2-methylbut-1-ene reacts with acidified manganate(VII) ions, under specific conditions, to produce two organic compounds **X** and **Y**.

**X** immediately reacts with the acidified manganate(VII) ions to form carbon dioxide and water. **Y** has the structural formula $\text{CH}_3\text{CH}_2\text{COCH}_3$.

